#!/bin/bash
# CheckMK Agent Plugin: DNF Update Check
#
# Checks for available package updates on RPM-based distributions.
# Supports: Red Hat Enterprise Linux 8-10 and compatible distributions
#           (AlmaLinux, Rocky Linux, Oracle Linux, CentOS Stream)
# Package managers: dnf (RHEL 8-10), dnf5 (Fedora 41+), yum (as dnf wrapper)
#
# Output format (<<<dnf>>> section):
#   Line 1: Reboot required for a newer kernel (yes/no)
#   Line 2: Number of available updates (-1 on error)
#   Line 3: Number of security updates [-1 error, -2 unsupported] [comma-separated list]
#   Line 4: Unix timestamp of last update (-1 if unknown)
#   Line 5: Unix timestamp of the newest repository metadata refresh (-1 if none)
#   Line 6: Unix timestamp since when no background refresh has completed
#           (-1 if the last one completed)
#   Line 7: Reboot hint from needs-restarting: "yes <comma-separated list>",
#           "no" or "unknown"
#
# Lines 2-4 and 7 come from a cache so the agent never waits on dnf. When the
# package state changes or the host reboots, a detached background run
# (--refresh) recomputes them within REFRESH_TIMEOUT. After a failed or
# unfinished refresh, the next one starts after RETRY_INTERVAL at the
# earliest. Lines 1, 5 and 6 are computed on every run.
